#### Non-Blocking Note
- In [`io_designs.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-design-merge/concurrency/benches/io_designs.rs#L43-L50), `io-workers` is parsed only when `backend.ends_with("-mux")` and is clamped via `workers.min(connections)` inside [`io_mux::run`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-design-merge/concurrency/benches/support/io_mux.rs#L42) after the echo listener thread starts (passing `--io-workers=0` on a `-mux` backend would panic at modulo division after spawning the listener thread). This is purely a manual CLI edge case on an internal benchmark target and not a blocker.
